WEBVTT

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.980
I possess the intellect of the gods!

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.880
I am the Phi-Brain, Orpheus.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.460
Jin...

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.290
Wh-what is this...?!

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.310
Jin?!

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:11.970
Become a Phi-Brain

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:21.920
What the heck was that?

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.790
The future... The future of ruin...

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.710
What happened, Kaito?

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.140
Hey, Kaito! What just happened?

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.710
Answer me, Kaito!

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:41.510
Jin...

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.280
Kaito, the person standing 
before you isn’t Jin!

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.220
He’s Orpheus!

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.300
Orpheus?!

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:54.610
Wh-who the heck’s this Orpheus guy?

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.990
I’ll explain later! There 
is no telling what he’ll do.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.250
For now, you need to get away from there!

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.180
Isn’t this...?

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.820
That’s impossible! Why?!

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:21.930
Raetsel!

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.140
Rae-Rae!

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.690
Raetsel...

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:39.740
Raetsel!

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.820
Raetsel!

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.080
N-no...

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.560
W-was that the future?

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:55.640
No, it wasn’t...

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.340
Raetsel... Where is Raetsel?!

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.400
I don’t believe it! She can’t be...!

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.820
Rae-Rae!

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:09.930
Raetsel!

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.350
Where were your brains, Kaito?

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:15.660
You could have saved Raetsel!

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.150
If you used the remote to

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:22.220
drop the iron ball back there, 
Raetsel would still be...!

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.990
This isn’t real!

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.420
It can’t be real!

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:31.660
Kaito?

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:34.280
Are you all right? What’s the matter?

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.010
As suspected, it still isn’t perfect.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.080
That’s the limit of what I can do.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:48.030
Wh-what is going on here?

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.450
What nonsense is this?

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.270
He isn’t Jin Makata?

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.270
He’s Orpheus?

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.330
What are you blathering on about?

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.300
Is-isn’t this...?

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.510
What’s the matter, Zagadka?

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:22.460
Lovushka!

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:27.310
If you don’t hurry, I’m going to 
eat everything in the picnic basket!

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:32.110
Lovushka!

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.030
Lovushka!

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.640
What is it?

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:39.290
You can be so silly!

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.320
Lovushka!

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:55.970
What’s gotten into Enigma?

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.330
He... also saw something!

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:03.690
You should be able to tell:

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.950
That was no mere illusion.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:12.570
If you serve me, regaining 
that warmth is no dream.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:20.250
Are-are you implying that you could 
bring Lovushka back from the dead?

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.100
Please wait!

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:22.730
Jin!

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:24.530
Wait!

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:36.050
Jin! Raetsel!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:07:03.270
Say, isn’t Orpheus the ancient big 
shot whom the Orpheus Order worshipped?

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:07.530
Doesn’t he appear as a 
minstrel in Greek mythology?

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.670
But I’m not sure if this 
is the same Orpheus or not...

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:17.630
It is clear that he is a 
genius from ancient times.

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:20.280
He created the Puzzle of God 
and the Armlets of Orpheus.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:23.540
He made the Puzzle of God? Really?

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:27.100
And he’s taken over Jin’s body?!

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.470
I’m havin’ a hard time buying this.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:32.610
Yeah. The very idea of taking 
over someone’s body!

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.430
That isn’t possible.

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:39.930
The Puzzle of God is a system designed 
to allow Orpheus to obtain immortality.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:41.690
Immortality?

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.690
According to the Pythagoras Document,

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:50.040
Orpheus found a means to cast off 
his body and exist in mind only.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:52.950
When battling in the Puzzle of God,

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:56.090
the puzzlers draw infinitely 
close to becoming Phi-Brains.

00:07:56.550 --> 00:08:01.210
Orpheus’ mind is downloaded into 
the person he chooses as his vessel.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:05.710
That is the true purpose 
behind the Puzzle of God.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:07.020
Say what?!

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.810
You download his mind?!

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:11.060
That’s just not possible!

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.440
What type of system would he even use?

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:17.580
It’s testimony to how Orpheus 
is an even greater genius

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.350
than we could begin to imagine.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:24.160
If that’s all true, 
what’s the Book of God?

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:28.140
From the beginning, the 
Book of God never existed.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:31.650
In other words, it was nothing more than bait

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:34.360
to encourage people to 
challenge the Puzzle of God.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:36.620
That’s horrible!

00:08:37.210 --> 00:08:43.300
Didn’t the POG try to raise Phi-Brains 
in the hopes of obtaining the Book of God?

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:48.020
That’s what Mom and Dad died for...?!

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.160
Kaito...

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:52.850
Orpheus has been manipulating...

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:54.730
all of us.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:57.880
Just so he could come back to life!

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.640
And what happened to Jin-Jin?

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.890
It’s not as though Jin had 
actually lost his memories.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:09.150
What do you mean by that?

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.330
He hadn’t truly lost his memories?

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:19.880
He sealed my mind within himself 
along with his own memories

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.880
in an attempt to prevent my resurrection.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:25.160
I can’t believe it!

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:29.830
Then does that mean Orpheus 
got resurrected because I

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.980
made Jin unlock his memories?

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:35.770
And what was that illusion Kaito saw?

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:37.300
According to the Pythagoras Document,

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:42.220
a perfect Phi-Brain can 
not only see the future,

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.020
but also surpass time, 
allowing him to see the past.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.560
He isn’t limited to looking.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:53.070
He can even interact with the 
past to change the future.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:58.450
Humans transcending time?! 
That’s preposterous!

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:03.700
But Orpheus has not yet 
become a perfect Phi-Brain.

00:10:04.550 --> 00:10:06.970
That is why he is only 
able to show illusions.

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:10.340
Orpheus showed you what the world could

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.930
have been like had he interfered.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.350
But that could have just been hypnosis.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:17.520
There’s even the possibility 
that this was some sort of trick.

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.320
That wasn’t an illusion...

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:25.720
So what would happen if Orpheus 
became a true Phi-Brain?

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:29.170
The world would be destroyed.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:38.990
So if you could change the past, 
would I get to see Lovushka?

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:43.240
If you want her back, serve me.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.020
Lovushka...

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:57.010
There is somebody I’d 
like to get back as well.

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:01.610
Raetsel?!

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:14.290
It’d destroy the world?

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:20.740
That’s what we saw happen 
the moment Orpheus awakens...

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:23.890
It’s the future of ruin...

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.610
Didn’t you see it as well, Kaito?

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:27.660
Yeah.

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:30.980
If three people who are close

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:34.170
to becoming Phi-Brains 
all saw the same future,

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.840
then it must be true.

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:40.170
B-but can’t we change that future?

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:43.440
Kaito’s changed the future 
once before, remember?

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:45.020
But that was...

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.100
Kaito Daimon!

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:49.420
Raetsel!

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.190
You made it outta there okay?

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.910
Where are you?

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:55.190
Together with Orpheus.

00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:56.450
What?

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:57.830
You’re with Orpheus?

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:00.790
I have a message from him.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:02.700
Rae-Rae...

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:06.380
Jin’s mind hasn’t vanished yet.

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:13.390
Jin’s... still alive!

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.100
You mean it?

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:16.130
I do.

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:20.260
And there’s only one way to save Jin.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:21.940
What is it?

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:27.820
Me, Kaito, Rook, Freecell and Gammon.

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:32.650
One out of us five must 
awaken as a Phi-Brain

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:36.290
and offer our brain to Orpheus as his vessel.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.650
If we do, he will release Jin.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.920
Is Jin... Is Jin really...?

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:48.350
If you want to get Jin back, 
come to the Republic of Amgine.

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:52.380
Then challenge the puzzles 
that Orpheus has prepared

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:54.190
and awaken as a Phi-Brain.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:58.140
Do you believe everything 
Orpheus has told you?

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:03.100
Yes. If it will save Jin, I’ll do it.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:04.990
I cannot allow that!

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:09.930
I’m sure you saw it--that future of ruin.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.680
We cannot allow Orpheus to run free!

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.590
For one thing, there is no guarantee that

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:19.350
he was telling the truth 
that this will save Jin!

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:20.690
Rook...

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:25.330
Then what do you suggest? There 
isn’t any other way to save Jin!

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:27.950
Without Jin,

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.010
all of the futures are the same to me...

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:35.960
This is foolish!

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:38.710
Jin!

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:42.900
Having been born on this world,

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.720
you must challenge the gods and surpass them!

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.610
That is the path mankind is meant to follow.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:55.730
I shall solve the puzzle created by 
the gods known as the “world.”

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:58.700
In doing so, I will obtain 
power that surpasses theirs.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.730
I will sacrifice as many lives as it takes!

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:21.130
I swear that I will get Jin back!

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:25.130
If it’d bring him back, I’d 
sell my soul to the devil!

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:29.010
Then become a Phi-Brain.

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:33.240
And then offer yourself to me.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:40.450
That wasn’t Jin!

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:53.910
Rook, I’m going to Amgine.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:55.290
Kaito!

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.730
I’m of a similar mind as Raetsel.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.890
If I can save Jin...

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:09.010
Bishop, ask the surrounding 
countries for their assistance

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.390
in keeping a close watch on Amgine.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:13.150
Certainly!

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:15.330
Rook?

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:20.810
As I’ve said, regardless 
of who sacrifices himself,

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:23.320
there is no guarantee that it will save Jin!

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:26.320
Then what am I supposed to do?

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:29.500
Search for a different way to save Jin.

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:30.660
Makes sense.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.440
The POG has contacts in various nations

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:36.330
with dominant figures from around the world.

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.730
We could keep the Republic of Amgine

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.200
under tabs if we sought their help.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:43.670
You mean to trap Orpheus there and

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:46.090
then search for a way to 
save Jin, don’t you?

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:48.950
But do you think you’ll find a way?

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:50.540
I don’t know.

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:54.100
What if... you don’t find a way...?

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:57.630
When that time comes, I will 
have no choice but to...

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:04.620
Rook, you bastard!

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:06.210
It cannot be helped.

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:08.480
Are you serious, Principal?!

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:13.740
If that is the only way to stop the 
future of ruin from coming to pass...

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.990
Not you too, Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:17.430
Do you think...

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:20.910
Do you think I’d let you do that?!

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:22.470
Kaito!

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:23.870
Kaito, stop it!

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:31.630
Didn’t Jin save both of us?!

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:36.300
Because Jin was there--because 
Jin guided us--

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.100
we are where we are now.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:43.320
Then isn’t it our turn to save Jin?!

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:44.150
You’re right.

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:49.960
That’s precisely why we must 
deal with this personally!

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:55.210
Jin Makata is dear to me; no 
one could ever replace him.

00:16:56.170 --> 00:17:00.220
But I am currently the POG’s director.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.640
I am responsible for coping with 
what the POG has brought upon us.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:22.730
Kaito!

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:51.610
Kaito...

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:54.890
Rook is also...

00:17:57.270 --> 00:17:58.480
I’m sure Rook is also--

00:17:58.480 --> 00:17:59.760
I know!

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:04.360
He’s grown strong, hasn’t he?

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.350
Kaito...

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:16.250
But you know, I still can’t bring 
myself to leave Jin to his fate...

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:17.700
But what can you do?

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:19.820
Remember what Orpheus said?

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:21.320
Freecell...

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:25.090
He said he would solve the puzzle called

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:27.400
the “world” and obtain 
the power of the gods.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:31.670
And he was willing to sacrifice 
as many lives as it takes.

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:36.070
Yeah, but I didn’t really 
get what he meant by that.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:39.080
I don’t know exactly what it means myself.

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:43.650
But if someone beats him to 
awakening as a perfect Phi-Brain

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:48.410
and is able to solve the puzzle of the world,

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:51.500
we could prevent the future 
of ruin from ever happening!

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:55.880
But if what Orpheus said is true,

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.570
won’t he just take over your body?

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:01.340
If you obtain power that surpasses his,

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.340
you may be able to stop him!

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:05.840
I guess that’s a possibility...

00:19:07.440 --> 00:19:08.500
I get it!

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.930
In short, I just gotta win!

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:13.660
What?!

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:18.080
I have no idea what how much 
of what he says is legit,

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:21.900
but long story short, isn’t he 
challenging me to a puzzle battle?

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:25.720
In that case, I just gotta 
beat him with puzzles!

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:27.770
Wait, Kaito! Don’t tell me you’re...?

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:30.410
Yeah, I’m goin’...

00:19:30.950 --> 00:19:32.200
to Amgine!

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.070
I-I knew it!

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:37.380
I shall accompany you, Kaito.

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.820
I’d like to help you out.

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:43.820
Freecell...

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:46.300
W-wait one darn minute!

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:48.660
There’s no way Rook will let you go!

00:19:49.220 --> 00:19:51.390
Money! How will you pay for this?

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:54.010
Leave that to me, Nonoha.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:56.920
Easy to say, but how are you 
going to cover this, Freecell?

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:08.030
How are you enjoying my personal 
jet, Pretty Melancholy?

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:10.180
It-it’s unnerving...

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.440
The food’s good, Kaito.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.830
Melancholy, thanks a bunch.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:22.260
It’s nothing!

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:24.370
Hardly even worthy of a word of thanks!

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:28.690
I saw that future as well.

00:20:30.430 --> 00:20:31.620
Melancholy, you did?

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:35.130
If that future comes to pass,

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:39.020
there goes all of my plans 
for a bright future!

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.740
I really appreciate it, Melancholy.

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:49.140
It’s not as though I’ve 
forgiven you yet, Freecell.

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:53.290
If you want me to truly forgive you,

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:57.400
defeat that Orpheus guy and 
come back safe and sound.

00:20:57.750 --> 00:20:58.890
Do you hear me?

00:20:59.790 --> 00:21:01.660
Thank you, Melancholy.

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:48.370
We’re here, Kaito!

00:21:48.750 --> 00:21:49.450
Yeah!

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:52.170
This is the Republic of Amgine!

00:21:54.300 --> 00:21:57.000
Let’s go, Kaito! Nonoha!

00:22:13.070 --> 00:22:15.020
Wh-what happened?

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:21.290
Jeez! Wait up, Kaito!

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:25.500
Not in your dreams!

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:27.510
Hey! I said to wait up!

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:29.840
Kaito!

00:24:01.930 --> 00:24:07.180
Kaito Daimon, can you solve 
my ultimate 3D puzzle?!

00:24:07.310 --> 00:24:08.610
Who are you?!

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:11.560
I am the Student Council President 
and President of the Puzzle Club!

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:14.750
I’m the top idol at Root 
Gakuen, Rook Banjo Crossfield!

00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:14.750
I solved it!

00:24:14.750 --> 00:24:16.190
What?! That quickly?!

00:24:16.360 --> 00:24:19.450
Next time, “It’s Okay If 
I Can’t Solve Puzzles.”

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:27.970
It’s Okay If I Can’t Solve Puzzles

00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:22.190
I won’t accept this reality!

00:24:22.530 --> 00:24:24.950
Nah, this is okay in its own right.

00:24:24.950 --> 00:24:26.580
Kaito?!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
I Didn’t See the Future Fin
